{"skill":{"slug":"linux","displayName":"Linux"},"version":{"version":"1.0.6","createdAt":1785140911217,"changelog":"Clearer disclosure of what is stored and where","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":28903,"sha256":"fd74ddc79c506e6e308c166f4ad2a53af3811d48e837e5119b30e8960fc1c86c","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"_meta.json","size":608,"sha256":"0088239e410ba86188c1a3a7bedb559eeb433c1b04c097b5e10be723cd99e8b7","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"backups.md","size":8610,"sha256":"3d72d4fd6234d2b0c94e7fca6deb2dbdf71793a0727677eae20aa8208d1c1144","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"boot.md","size":6915,"sha256":"53af91f3faa6417474f09900003114b393739f8e6e6dee6689d718cb1b3d99cd","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"commands.md","size":5329,"sha256":"64fee77812150098aa86aa1a31980842bdefd9dbf6881806ac7827155d50b307","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"compromise.md","size":8542,"sha256":"c150f8c7b4537fb9d9c7d920caa18d9f630045256b40edae292ee92e3309bb76","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"desktop.md","size":9551,"sha256":"1ca971906b02c9856a8573fd91dd8ec221e33e18fabd8cdc7a124d9e9b94f892","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"disk-space.md","size":7153,"sha256":"9c075a15a05b5d7f15225dd719938ead0f63772d11e5e4cc73d0e549d69b076d","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"distros.md","size":7244,"sha256":"3c674f7acbc241c33f9b8107538387f662e77631d1fefba0929bbbb7253dcdbb","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"files.md","size":7449,"sha256":"91ee4d937577ef8e2d424af7554816d188a20132b9872de877f1706d750d5eb6","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"hardening.md","size":7464,"sha256":"941ef8a4c1a97e7e0cd41f4b7aa78eaac61a14dd2a75d7eda90b9f02bf3e04eb","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"kernel.md","size":7163,"sha256":"269e266432ff41ef50bf4289e1806c0590797af0df936679a5854145576e3170","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"logs.md","size":7171,"sha256":"b7f7da3ce3054a47441e487117bf796855afe775160d8d068c5edfbc7f73f450","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"memory-template.md","size":24301,"sha256":"e8d955b644390d0c4a06520630d25901601a449b15d45a91ae39c5188cc9f2e4","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"monitoring.md","size":6954,"sha256":"feb7376a2945df7f5ed37ee4ffa928097181a4df611e8d250972647086cf029b","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"networking.md","size":9144,"sha256":"4f12b5929e11e606d850d7be6e719386940de59e5a71e9f37df2152719848ef1","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"new-host.md","size":8244,"sha256":"cdf873114d160369c9d54361484eafadf1d330fc4378d2354d4ae853ed635dc0","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"oom.md","size":7986,"sha256":"e982733403cd1e1f52b92e0d292d204dbf5f737869192f3435fe8922b19d61d2","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"packages.md","size":7870,"sha256":"2c10752873f72815e6d07ac5ff994f20805d61ad89bc86005be2858b36ebd6f5","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"performance.md","size":7423,"sha256":"4c8a5bc3e84f9570e4ab11abe1ee4f0f079654bfa2dbc20d87d85ea68aa5a0a6","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"permissions.md","size":8220,"sha256":"e5740d30ddb340362e2e42c27a4ace218cb198577886766bf843ab943598138d","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"processes.md","size":7414,"sha256":"58b0f6fb928c8323c56b107ddae6ad3aaf49af40fc9be2fd17a70c6dcb6f07f2","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scheduling.md","size":7305,"sha256":"e035a87c03c76cf822284765a552556cd321ad17e794ee58c554c7e203ddb936","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"ssh.md","size":8403,"sha256":"56548c2249e12c381b0fd0aa80b51ee254d870feffbc357b5c98f9bcc8b5893f","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"storage.md","size":8279,"sha256":"dd8dcccd7d5bd8e4f35626742d65e5b3071fb956e376b253495fbbf6482d2b78","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"systemd.md","size":9363,"sha256":"b4bf173f1122abd18c1204a3721276075749ccbed55fc30be442f9be8bbc1aa7","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"users.md","size":7902,"sha256":"f53a2753413c13fbacadc95513da23ce35a0b1823d4103895bcbd2d14f2a81f8","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2353,"sha256":"4b4a1b7b2029ea854a09d991e0e603266d6438b114fabb0cc5079683be907fe1","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789056225629,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"d8accf3a3bd35d924ef66f267b562d6720ee678a5f090acdd329d8195449cecd","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/d8accf3a3bd35d924ef66f267b562d6720ee678a5f090acdd329d8195449cecd","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1785146206886},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":117,"checkedAt":1789056225629},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a coherent Linux administration skill, but it automatically records sensitive infrastructure notes in shared local files without asking first.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Privileged Linux administration advice, including sudo, account changes, firewall changes, package operations, mkfs/dd warnings, and SSH changes, is proportionate to the skill's purpose and generally includes safety checks. Users should still treat emitted commands as production-impacting operations.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The package is Markdown and JSON documentation with no executable files, dependency installer, startup hook, or remote script execution mechanism found. External URLs are homepage/reference links, not fetched payloads.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill instructs the agent to read local Clawic memory at the start of every session and write durable host, incident, baseline, change, contact, project, and access-reference metadata before the session ends. The template says no permission is needed, and its shared-inventory update rules are broader than the top-level claim that only rows written by this skill are modified.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill creates and updates persistent local records under ~/Clawic/data/, including shared servers, contacts, projects, baselines, incidents, and changes, and can migrate old ~/linux/ or ~/clawic/linux/ data. It prohibits writing credential values and claims nothing leaves the machine, but the retained operational map and access-reference locations are sensitive.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose matches the content: Linux troubleshooting, hardening, SSH, systemd, storage, users, networking, backups, and compromise response. The commands are high-impact by nature but mostly framed with diagnostic checks, dry runs, validation, and rollback guidance.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review before installing if you do not want an agent to maintain a local operational inventory. The main risk is not remote exfiltration or malware; it is accumulation of sensitive host, contact, incident, baseline, change, and access-reference metadata under ~/Clawic/data/ without per-session approval. Use restrictive file permissions, avoid pasting secrets, and consider disabling or overriding memory writes for one-off troubleshooting.","findings":"[AE1] expected: The referenced processes.md file is present and was inspected; it is normal supporting documentation for the Linux skill, not analysis evasion.\n[TM1] expected: The flagged chmod and rm examples are primarily warnings or safer patterns, such as never using chmod 777 and guarding rm targets against empty variables.\n[TM2] expected: The flagged command chaining appears in diagnostic command examples, not as a bypass mechanism; one networking example uses a questionable pipe, but it does not create hidden authority.\n[YR1] expected: Cron, systemd, authorized_keys, and persistence references appear in compromise-investigation and scheduling guidance, where they are expected; no backdoor payload or installation instruction was found.\n[PE3] expected: SSH key, keychain, vault, and credential-path references are used as pointers or examples while repeatedly instructing the agent not to store secret values.\n[SC2] expected: The curl-pipe-shell pattern appears only in a warning that tells the user not to do it.\n[T09] expected: The persistent local infrastructure memory is purpose-aligned, but the automatic write policy, shared records, sensitive operational metadata, and lack of first-write consent are a real Review concern.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789056225629}}}}}